$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(6-(6-Chloropyrazin-2-yl)benzo[d]thiazol-2-yl)acetamide (56).
2,6-Dichloropyrazine (55, 1.119 g, 7.511 mmol), 4a (3.07 g, 9.65 mmol),
Pd(dppf)2Cl2/DCM complex (519.9 mg, 0.637 mmol), and K2CO3 (2.992 g,
21.65 mmol) were suspended in 1,2-dimethoxyethane (50 mL), and H2O (15
mL) was added. The flask was fitted with a reflux condenser and placed in
a preheated oil bath (90 °C) and stirred under N2. After 1.5 h, the
mixture was cooled to room temperature and filtered, and the solid was
washed with 1,2-dimethoxyethane. The solid was set aside, and the
filtrate was concentrated, treated with Et2O, and filtered. The solid
from this filtration was washed with Et2O, H2O, and three cycles of MeOH
and Et2O. The solid was collected and dried to afford 56 (1.954 g, 73%
purity, 62% yield). For characterization purposes, a portion (~100 mg)
was purified on HPLC (10% → 95% MeCN/H2O with 0.1% TFA over 30 min). The
fractions with product were collected, concentrated, and washed with
Et2O, MeOH, and Et2O. The solid was collected and dried under high vacuum
in a H2O bath (50 °C). MS (ESI pos ion) m/z: 305 (M + H+). 1H NMR (400
MHz, DMSO-d 6, δ): 12.50 (s, 1H), 9.32 (s, 1H), 8.77 (s, 1H), 8.72 (s,
1H), 8.20 (d, J = 8.53 Hz, 1H), 7.86 (d, J = 8.53 Hz, 1H), 2.23 (s, 3H).
