$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
compounds 3, 4, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12 and 13: A mixture of the amines 1a-b or
amides 6a-c or 7a-c (0.43 mmol), boronic acids 2a-q (1.3mmol), Pd(PPh3)4
(0.043 mmol), and Na2CO3 (2.1mmol) in 5 mL of a mixture of DME/H2O (3:1)
in coated Kimble vials was stirred with orbital stirring at 110 °C for
12h. The resulting mixture was concentrated in vacuo and then Ethyl
Acetate was added. This solution was washed with water and NaOH 1N to
remove the acid boronic excess. The organic layer was collected, dried
over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified
by column chromatography or preparative method on silica gel.
N-(4,6-di(thiophen-2-yl)pyrimidin-2-yl)acetamide (8o), yield 62%. Mp
173-175 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ (ppm): 2.54 (3H, s, CH3), 7.01 (2 x 1H, m,
thiophene), 7.33 (1H, s, H5), 7.36 (2 x 1H, m, thiophene), 7.65 (2x 1H,
m, thiophene), 7.79 (1H, s, NH). MS m/z: 301 (59). HRMS (EI) calculated
for C14H11N3OS2 301.0344, found 301.0349.
