$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
4,5-Bis(2,5-dimethylthiophen-3-yl)-2,2’-bithiophene (L1-O) To solution
mixture of BPin-Th-DTE (1 g, 2.3 mmol), 2-bromothiophene (815 mg, 5 mmol)
and tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (135 mg, 0.12 mmol) in
degassed THF (75 mL) was added aqueous cesium carbonate solution (2 M,
3.03 g, 4.65 mL, 9.3 mmol). The progress of the reaction was monitored by
TLC. The reaction mixture was then extracted with chloroform, washed with
brine, and finally dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. After
filtration and removal of the solvent, the crude product was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel (70-230 mesh) using n-hexane as the
eluent. The desired product was collected as the second fraction. Further
purification was achieved by recrystallization from hot n-hexane to give
the product.
4’,5’-Bis(2,5-dimethylthiophen-3-yl)-5-bromo-2,2’-bithiophene
(5-Br-Th-Th-DTE) This was synthesized according to a procedure similar to
that of 4,5-bis(2,5-dimethylthiophen-3-yl)-2,2’-bithiophene except
2,5-dibromothiophene (1.2 g, 5 mmol) was used instead of
2-bromothiophene. A white solid was obtained. Yield: 665 mg, 62 %. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K): δ 2.02 (s, 3H, -Me), 2.04 (s, 3H, -Me), 2.37 (s,
3H, -Me), 2.38 (s, 3H, -Me), 6.44 (s, 1H, thienyl), 6.48 (s, 1H,
thienyl), 6.90 (d, J HH = 3.8 Hz, 1H, thienyl), 6.98 (d, J HH = 3.8 Hz,
1H, thienyl), 7.03 (s, 1H, thienyl). 13C{1H} NMR (100.6 MHz, CDCl3, 298
K, relative to Me4Si): δ 13.82, 13.97, 15.16, 15.19, 110.80, 123.50,
126.47, 126.91, 127.36, 129.98, 130.66, 132.73, 133.17, 133.51, 134.09,
134.53, 134.99, 135.52, 135.69, 138.88. Positive FAB-MS: m/z 466 {M}+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Gated Photochromism in Triarylborane-Containing Dithienylethenes: A New
Approach to a "Lock-Unlock" System
