$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure B. 25. Boronic acid (0.75 mmol, 1
equiv), aryl bromide or triflate (0.9-1.3 equiv), and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphane)palladium(0) (43 mg, 37.5 μmol, 5 mol %) were
suspended in 1.5 mL of DMF in a 10 mL septum-capped tube containing a
stirring magnet. To this was added a solution of NaHCO3 (189 mg, 2.25
mmol, 3 equiv) in 1.5 mL of water, and the vial was sealed with an Teflon
cap. The mixture was irradiated with microwaves for 15 min at a
temperature of 150 °C with an initial irradiation power of 100 W. After
the reaction, the vial was cooled to 40 °C, the crude mixture was
partitioned between ethyl acetate and water, and the aqueous layer was
extracted three times with ethyl acetate. The combined organic layers
were dried over MgSO4, and the solvents were removed in vacuo. The
coupling products were obtained after flash chromatography on silica gel
(petroleum ether/ethyl acetate mixtures) and/or crystallization.
9-Isoquinolin-4-yl-1,2,6,7-tetrahydro-5H-pyrido[3,2,1-ij]quinolin-3-one
(14). Compound 14 was obtained according to procedure B from 5a (266 mg,
1.0 mmol) and 4-isoquinolineboronic acid (227 mg, 0.9 mmol) after flash
chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate, 2/3) and
crystallization from acetone/diethylether as colorless needles (173 mg,
0.55 mmol, 61%). R f = 0.10; mp 158- 159 °C. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
2.01 (m, 2H), 2.72 (m, 2H), 2.87 (t, 3 J = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 2.97 (m, 2H),
3.95 (t, 3 J = 6.0 Hz, 2H), 7.14 (s, 1H), 7.15 (s, 1H), 7.62 (m, 1H),
7.68 (m, 1H), 7.94 (d, 3 J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 8.03 (d, 3 J = 7.9 Hz, 1H),
8.45 (s, 1H), 9.23 (s, 1H). 13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 21.4, 25.3,
27.4, 31.5, 40.0, 124.7, 125.5, 125.6, 127.1, 127.4, 127.9, 128.4, 129.3,
130.5, 131.1, 132.6, 134.2, 136.0, 142.8, 151.9, 169.5. MS m/z 315.10
(MH+). Purity by LC/MS: 100% (Rt = 9.71 min). Anal. calcd. for
(C21H18N2O) C 80.23, H 5.77, N 8.91; found C 80.16, H 5.59, N 8.88.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (100W), Suzuki coupling, sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fine-Tuning the Selectivity of Aldosterone Synthase Inhibitors:
Structure-Activity and Structure-Selectivity Insights from Studies of
Heteroaryl Substituted 1,2,5,6-Tetrahydropyrrolo[3,2,1-ij]quinolin-4-one
Derivatives
