$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for C-5 arylation of
2,3-disubstituted N-methyl-7-azaindole (Procedure D)
5-(4-Methoxyphenyl)-1-methyl-2-phenyl-3-p-tolyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine
(5a): A solution of
5-bromo-1-methyl-2-phenyl-3-(p-tolyl)-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine (50 mg,
0.13 mmol), 4-methoxyphenylboronic acid (22.17 mg 0.14 mmol), Pd(OAc)2
(1.47 mg, 0.006 mmol), dppf ( 6.95 mg, 0.01mmol), and Cs2CO3 (129.01 mg,
0.39 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane:water (0.5 mL, 3:1 mixture) was heated to 80 °C
for 6 h under N2 atmosphere. The reaction was cooled to room temperature,
diluted with EtOAc (30 mL) filtered through celite, and concentrated
under vacuum. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc, 96: 4). Compound 5a (38.6 mg, 72%) as a white solid.
4-(5-(benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)-2-(3-methoxyphenyl)-1-methyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridin-3-yl)benzonitrile
(5e) Synthesized from
4-(5-bromo-2-(3-methoxyphenyl)-1-methyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridin-3-yl)benzonitrile
(55 mg, 0.131 mmol), benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-ylboronic acid (26.1 mg, 0.157
mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (1.4 mg 0.006 mmol), dppf (7.2 mg 0.013 mmol) and Cs2CO3
(128.0 mg,0.393 mmol) by following procedure D. Purified by silica gel
column chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 95:5). Compound 5e (36.3 mg, 60%) as
a white solid. mp 200-201 0C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.58 (d, J = 2.0
Hz, 1H), 8.11 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H), 7.57 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 7.39 (d, J =
8.3 Hz, 3H), 7.37 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 7.07 (d,
J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.00 (dd, J = 8.2, 2.3 Hz, 1H), 6.94 (s, 1H), 6.92 (s,
1H), 6.87 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 2H), 3.83 (s, 3H), 3.78 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.7, 148.3, 147.1, 142.9, 139.6, 139.5, 133.6, 132.2,
132.1, 131.7, 130.7, 130.0, 129.6, 125.2, 123.0, 120.9, 119.2, 118.9,
116.4, 114.4, 111.56, 109.0, 108.8, 108.0, 101.2, 55.3, 29.8; HRMS (ESI):
calcd for C29H22N3O3 [M+H]+: 460.1656, found: 460.1680.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
