$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure. To a screw-capped vial was
added Pd(OAc)2 (6.0 mg, 0.025 mmol, 5 mol%), P(p-C6H4F)3 (16 mg, 0.05
mmol, 10 mol%), CsOH.H2O (168 mg, 1.0 mmol, 2 eq), and boronate ester 1
(155 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1 eq). The vial was sealed with a PTFE septum and
then evacuated and backfilled with N2 (this sequence was carried out
three times to ensure complete degassing of viscous liquids). Toluene (2
mL, anhydrous/degassed) was added via syringe through the septum,
followed by vigorous stirring and addition of the aryl bromide (0.55
mmol, 1.1 eq) was added via syringe [Note: Aryl bromides that were solids
were added with the other reagents prior to evacuation]. The sealed
reaction vessel was heated to 80 °C in an aluminum heating block for 16
h. At this time, the reaction was allowed to cool to room temperature and
was diluted with EtOAc. The resulting heterogeneous mixture was filtered
through a pad of Celite (eluted with additional EtOAc) and the eluent was
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude material was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel (heptanes/ethyl acetate) to afford
the 2-heteroaryl tetrahydropyridine products. The purified 2-heteroaryl
tetrahydropyridine was dissolved in EtOH (4 mL) followed by addition of
NH4CO2H (20 eq) and 10 wt % Pd/C (20 % relative to tetrahydropyridine). A
reflux condenser was attached and the reaction was heated to 65 °C for 16
h. At this time, the reaction was filtered through a thin pad of Celite
(eluted with additional EtOH), and all solvent removed under reduced
pressure. The residue was re-dissolved in a minimal amount of CH2Cl2, to
complete precipitation of excess NH4CO2H, followed by filtration through
Celite (eluted with additional CH2Cl2) and evaporation of all solvent to
afford the indicated α-heteroaryl piperidine products without additional
purification required (unless otherwise noted). 3b as an offwhite solid,
yield 60%. (mp = 130-132 °C). IR (film): 2937, 2862, 1682, 1588, 1460,
1366, 1155, 906, 726 cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.82 (d, J = 2.7 Hz, 1H),
7.79 (m, 1H), 6.57 (m, 1H), 5.36 (m, 1H), 4.01 (m, 1H), 3.25 (m, 4H),
2.73 (m, 1H), 2.23 (m, 1H), 1.97 (m, 4H), 1.84 (m, 1H), 1.63-1.46 (m,
3H), 1.43 (s, 9H), 1.40-1.34 (m, 1H); 13C{1H} NMR (CDCl3): δ 155.5,
143.7, 135.8, 135.3, 132.4, 116.2, 79.7, 51.7, 47.3, 40.2, 28.4, 28.0,
25.4, 25.3, 19.4. HRMS (ESI/[M+H]+) calcd. for C19H30N3O2: 332.2333.
Found: 332.2339.
