$DATUM A solution of
2-amino-6-iodo-3-(4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)quinazolin-4(3H)-one (59)
(0.100 g, 0.232 mmol),
N-(2,4-difluorophenyl)-2-methoxy-5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridine-3-sulfonamide
(73) (0.109 g, 0.255 mmol), Cs2CO3 (0.227 g, 0.696 mmol), and
PdCl2(dppf)-DCM adduct (0.019 g, 0.023 mmol) in 1,4-dioxane (0.928 ml)
and water (0.232 ml) was heated to 80°C for 1 hour. After cooling to room
temperature, the solution was diluted with EtOAc and washed with water,
brine, dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated onto celite. The residue was
purified with silica gel chromatography (50-100% EtOAc/hexanes) to give a
residue which was triturated with Et2O.
5-(2-amino-4-oxo-3-(4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl)-3,4-dihydroquinazolin-6-yl)-N-(2,4-difluorophenyl)-2-methoxypyridine-3-sulfonamide
(25) (0.083 g, 0.138 mmol, 59.3 % yield) as a light beige solid. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ ppm 10.19 (s, 1 H), 8.76 (d, J=2.54 Hz, 1 H), 8.16
(d, J=2.44 Hz, 1 H), 8.02 (d, J=2.34 Hz, 1 H), 7.87-7.99 (m, 3 H), 7.64
(d, J=8.19 Hz, 2 H), 7.20-7.36 (m, 3 H), 6.96-7.08 (m, 1 H), 6.60 (br.
s., 2 H), 3.97 (s, 3 H); HRMS calculated for C27H19N5O4F5S (M +1)+,
604.1078; found 604.1077.
