$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Table 1. An oven-dried
conical vial was cooled under a stream of argon and charged with a stir
bar, 2 (15.0 mg, 29.3 mmol), Pd2dba3 (1.1 mg, 1.2 mmol), SPhos (1.9 mg,
4.7 mmol), PhB(OH)2 (7.2 mg, 58.7 mmol), and K3PO4 (18.7 mg, 88.0 mmol).
The vial was sealed with a Biotage Reseal cap and flushed with argon for
5 min. Toluene (0.4 mL) was added through the septum and allowed to spin
for 5 min after which the reaction was heated to the indicated
temperature for 16 h. The reaction was cooled to room temperature and 3.0
mg of 1,10-phenanthroline was added to the reaction, as an internal
standard. The mixture was diluted with 1.5 mL of CH2Cl2 and a portion
injected onto a GC-MS. Solvent was removed from the remainder of the
solution and diluted to 1 mg/mL with MeCN. The MeCN solution was filtered
through a microfilter and a 100 mL portion injected onto a HPLC. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.71 (m, 1H), 7.49 (t, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.37 (d, J =
2.0 Hz, 1H), 6.65 (dd, J = 1.8, 0.7 Hz, 1H), 6.43 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1H),
5.61 (dd, J = 12.0, 4.9 Hz, 1H), 5.14 (m, 1H), 3.74 (s, 3H), 2.77 (m,
1H), 2.40 (dd, J = 13.6, 4.9 Hz, 1H), 2.30 (m, 2H), 2.16 (m, 3H), 2.15
(s, 3H), 1.81 (m, 1H), 1.64 (m, 3H), 1.48 (s, 3H), 1.13 (s, 3H). 13C NMR
(126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 201.91, 171.56, 171.14, 169.96, 145.23, 143.66,
141.72, 139.85, 119.03, 116.20, 109.73, 108.84, 74.99, 71.68, 64.03,
53.60, 52.02, 51.64, 43.02, 42.11, 38.19, 35.51, 30.75, 20.57, 18.16,
16.48, 15.13. HRMS: [M+Na]+ calcd 521.1788, found 521.1793. Melting
point: 235°C (dec.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective (labile acetate left intact), stereoselective
(stereoretention without epimerization), Suzuki-Miyaura reaction, sealed
tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-Catalyzed Transformations of Salvinorin A, a Neoclerodane
Diterpene from Salvia divinorum
