$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(R)-3-[1-(2,5-Difluorophenyl)ethoxy]-5-(3-methy1H-pyrazo4-yl)pyridin-2-amine
(6a). To a suspension of 11a (100 mg, 0.3 mmol),
3-methy4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole (158 mg,
0.76 mmol), and palladium tetrakis( triphenylphosphine) (35 mg, 0.03
mmol) in dioxane (12.5 mL) were added NaHCO3 (64 mg, 0.76 mmol) and water
(5 mL). The reaction mixture was thoroughly degassed. After being heated
at 110 °C for 90 min, the reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature
and partitioned between 10% citric acid solution (25 mL) and TBME (25
mL). The aqueous layer was made basic with ammonia and further extracted
with TBME (25 mL). The organic layer was then dried with MgSO4, filtered,
and evaporated. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography
over silica gel, eluted with 1/4 heptane/EtOAc followed by 100% EtOAc, to
provide the desired product 6a.
3-[(1R)-1-(5-Fluoro-2-methoxyphenyl)ethoxy]-5-(5-methy1H-pyrazo4-yl)pyridin-2-amine
(6c). In a similar manner to the preparation of 6a, 11c (250 mg, 0.66
mmol) was reacted with
3-methy4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole (239 mg,
1.15 mmol) to afford 6c (128 mg, 57% yield) as a pale, dense yellow foam
after purification. LC-MS (APCI) m/z 343 (M + H)+; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
methanod4) δ 7.53−7.42 (m, 2H), 7.08 (dd, J = 2.73, 8.98 Hz, 1H),
7.04−6.93 (m, 2H), 6.79 (d, J = 1.56 Hz, 1H), 5.78 (q, J = 6.51 Hz, 1H),
4.89 (br s, 2H), 3.89 (s, 3H), 2.10 (s, 3H), 1.64 (d, J = 6.25 Hz, 3H),
one NH proton is missing due to deuterium exchange.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Suzuki coupling
