$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of Methyl
3-[[6-(1H-Indo6-yl)indo1-yl]methyl]-benzoate (5). To a solution of
indole-6-boronic acid (274 mg, 1.7 mmol) and compound 4 (516 mg, 1.5
mmol) in THF (15 mL) was added Pd(PPh3)4 (87.2 mg, 0.075 mmol), followed
by K2CO3 (2.0 M, 3.0 mL). The mixture was stirred and heated to reflux
under argon for about 4 h. After the reaction was completed, the mixture
was cooled to room temperature, water (20.0 mL) was added, and the
product was extracted with ethyl acetate (20 mL × 3). The organic solvent
was combined, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered, and evaporated. The
crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography (20% EtOAc/
hexanes). Methyl 3-[[5-(1H-indo6-yl)indo1-yl]methyl] benzoate (5b).
Compound 5b was prepared using indole-6-boronic acid (90 mg, 0.55 mmol)
and compound 4b (172 mg, 0.5 mmol) following the same procedure described
for synthesis of 5. Pale yellow powder. Yield 106.4 mg, 56%. Data for 5c:
MS calcd for C25H20N2O2: 380.2; found: 381.1 (M+H)+; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
8.16 (br, 1H), 7.95 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 2H), 7.90 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 1H), 7.68
(d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 7.62 (s, 1H), 7.48 (dd, J = 8.6 Hz, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H),
7.43 (dd, J = 8.2 Hz, J = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7.37 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H),
7.33-7.26 (m, 2H), 7.21 (t, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H), 7.16 (d, J = 3.2 Hz, 1H),
6.61 (d, J = 3.0 Hz, 1H), 6.56 (s, 1H), 5.38 (s, 2H), 3.89 (s, 3H); 13C
NMR δ 166.82, 138.09, 137.01, 136.62, 135.61, 134.51, 131.37, 130.84,
129.45, 129.07, 129.01, 128.68, 128.14, 126.67, 124.35, 122.27, 120.76,
120.39, 119.76, 109.73, 109.66, 102.58, 102.47, 52.23, 50.04.
