$DATUM Heterotriangulene trimer (6): A flame-dried 50 mL Schlenk flask was
equipped with the monobromo trimer (200 mg, 0.17 mmol), bispinacolato
diboron (54 g, 0.21 mmol) and KOAc (60 mg, 0.61 mmol). The mixture was
suspended in anhydrous N,N-dimethylformamide (6 mL) and degassed with
argon for 1.5 hours. Subsequently,
[1,1'-bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene]dichloropalladium(II)
dichloromethane (8 mg, 6 mol%) was added and the resulting mixture was
stirred under an argon atmosphere at 85°C overnight. The reaction was
stopped by addition of water and the resulting mixture was extracted with
CH2Cl2 (3x). The combined organic fractions were dried with MgSO4,
filtered and the solvents were evaporated. The crude product was purified
by column chromatography (silica, n-hexane//CH2Cl2 2:1 to 1:1). 6 as a
colorless, crystalline solid, yield 116 mg, 56%. 1H NMR (CD2Cl2, 250 MHz,
δ): 1.30 (s, 12H) 1.56 (s, 12H), 1.65 (m, 36H), 1.74 (s, 6H), 7.07 (t, J1
= J2 = 7.5 Hz, 4H), 7.35 (m, 8H), 7.58 (d, J1 = 5 Hz, 8H), 7.76 (s, 2H).
13C NMR (CD2Cl2, 75 MHz, δ): 135.8, 135.6, 132.1, 131.5, 130.9, 130.7,
130.1, 126.7, 123.9, 123.4, 123.4, 122.2, 84.0, 83.3, 36.0, 33.4, 30.1,
25.1 (18 out of 20 expected). FD-MS (8kV): m/z = 1271.3 (100%, M+).
ESI-HR MS calcd for C87H88BN3O2 ([M+H]+) 1218.7048, found 1218.7054.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM π-Conjugated Heterotriangulene Macrocycles by Solution and
Surface-supported Synthesis toward Honeycomb Networks
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schluetter, Florian; Rossel, Frederic; Kivala, Milan; Enkelmann, Volker;
Gisselbrecht, Jean-Paul; Ruffieux, Pascal; Fasel, Roman; Muellen, Klaus
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(11), 4550-4557

