$DATUM 1-(Cyclohexylamino)-7-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-5H-pyrido[4,3-b]indole-4-carboxamide
(38): To a slurry containing 34 (50 mg, 0.146 mmol), Pd2(dba)3 (13 mg,
0.015 mmol), tricyclohexylphosphine (10 mg, 0.036 mmol) and tribasic
potassium phosphate (1.27 M in water, 0.389 mL, 0.495 mmol) in dioxane
(2.98 mL) was added
1-methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole (46
mg, 0.219 mmol). The slurry was sealed and purged with nitrogen gas for 5
minutes. The reaction was heated at 100 °C for 2 h until completion. The
reaction was cooled, treated with saturated sodium bicarbonate solution,
and extracted with ethyl acetate (3x). The combined organic layers were
dried with magnesium sulfate, filtered and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography to afford 38.
Yellow solid, yield 30 mg, 0.077 mmol, 53%. LRMS (ESI) calc'd for
(C22H25N6O) [M + H]+ 389.2, found 389.2. 1H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ
11.39 (s, 1H), 8.49 (s, 1H), 8.19 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.08 (s, 1H), 7.83
(s, 1H), 7.80 (s, 1H), 7.78 (brs, 1H), 7.40 (dd, J = 1.6, 8.2 Hz, 1H),
7.11 (brs, 1H), 6.15 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H), 4.32-4.21 (m, 1H), 3.87 (s,
3H), 2.00-1.94 (m, 2H), 1.80-1.73 (m, 2H), 1.67-1.61 (m, 1H), 1.56-1.48
(m, 2H), 1.40-1.32 (m, 2H), 1.22-1.17 (m, 1H).
