$DATUM Methyl (R)-1-Formyl-1,4,5,6-tetrahydro-[2,4'-bipyridine]-6-carboxylate
(6c) Methyl (R)-6-bromo-1-formyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydropyridine-2-carboxylate
3 (100 mg, 0.40 mmol) was dissolved in DMF (5 mL) and the
4-pyridylboronic acid (73 mg, 0.60 mmol) and Et3N (0.17 mL, 1.61 mmol)
were added. The flask was flushed with argon and the contents were
subjected to freeze, pump, and thaw cycles in order to degas it
completely. PdCl2(PPh3)2 (14.2 mg, 0.02 mmol) was added and the resulting
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 16 hours. The completion of
reaction was monitored by TLC. The reaction was quenched by addition of
water and extracted with dichloromethane. The combined organic phases
were dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate. After the drying agent was
filtered off, the filtrate was evaporated to dryness in vacuo, and the
residue was purified by column chromatography (EtOAc: n-pentane; 1:1) on
silica gel. Yellow oil; (52 mg, 53%). [α]D = +7.8 (c = 1, CHCl3). Rf 0.64
(EtOAc: n-pentane; 1:4).1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 8.58-8.57 (m, 2H,
CH), 8.17 (s, 1H, CHO), 7.36-7.31 (m, 2H,CH), 5.42 (m, 1H, CH), 5.28 (m,
1H, CH), 3.72 (s, 3H, COOCH3), 2.41 (m, 1H, CH2), 2.26-2.18 (m, 2H, CH2),
1.87 (m, 1H, CH2). 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CDCl3) δ 170.5 (COO), 160.6 (CHO),
150.4 (2 x CH), 144.2 (C), 135.4 (C), 122.1 (2 x CH), 115.3 (CH), 52.7
(CHCOO), 50.1 (COOCH3), 23.6 (CH2), 20.6 (CH2). C13H14N2O3 (246.10). HRMS
(EI): m/z = 246.09994; calcd.: m/z = 246.09989.
