$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(2R,3R)-2-(2,4-difluorophenyl)-3-(2-(pyridin-4-yl)-4,5-dihydrothieno[2,3-c]pyridin-6(7H)-yl)-1-(1H-1,2,4-triazol-1-yl)butan-2-ol
(57a). A mixture of 56 (120.00 mg, 0.26mmol), Cesium carbonate (169.43
mg, 0.52 mmol), 4-pyridinylboronic acid (40.26 mg, 0.33 mmol) and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (0) (29.63 mg, 0.02 mmol) in
dioxane (10 ml) and H2O (4 ml) was degassed and flushed with argon. The
mixture was heated at 80 °C for 10 h. The solvent was evaporated under
reduced pressure. The residue was diluted with H2O (20 ml) and extracted
with ethyl acetate (30 ml ×2). The combined organic layers were washed
with H2O (15 ml ×2) and brine (15 ml ×2), dried over anhydrous Na2SO4,
and filtrated, then the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure.
The residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography (CH2Cl2 :
MeOH 200:1∼100:1) afforded compound. Yield: (63.70 mg, 53.2%), pale
yellow solid. mp 116-118 °C. [α]22D -24.0° (c 0.125, CHCl3). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.54 (d, J = 6.2 Hz, 2H), 7.92 (s, 1H), 7.78 (s, 1H),
7.52-7.44 (m, 1H), 7.39 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 2H), 7.20 (s, 1H), 6.82-6.70 (m,
2H), 4.90 (q, J = 14.9 Hz, 2H), 4.05 (d, J = 14.9 Hz, 1H), 3.76 (d, J =
15.0 Hz, 1H), 3.29-3.13 (m, 2H), 2.96-2.68 (m, 3H), 1.02 (d, J = 5.5 Hz,
3H). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3): δ 151.60, 148.10, 146.54, 144.26, 137.30,
132.68, 130.76, 130.56, 124.77, 124.66 (2C, overlap), 124.19, 123.67,
111.51, 104.16, 78.73, 63.85, 55.94 (2C, overlap), 55.88, 26.59, 7.38. MS
(ESI) m/z: 468.2 (M+1)+. HRMS (ESI): Anal. Calcd for C24H24F2N5OS:
468.1635, Found: 468.1626.
