$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A suspension of
6-bromo-4-(2-ethylbutylamino)-2-methylquinoline-3-carbonitrile (150 mg,
0.43 mmol), 3-pyridinylboronic acid (64 mg, 0.52 mmol) and sodium
carbonate (70 mg, 0.65 mmol) in dioxane:water (9:1, 5 mL) was purged with
nitrogen for 10 min. Tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (50 mg, 0.04
mmol) was added to the mixture and heated to 90 °C for 3 h. The reaction
mixture was then concentrated to get a residue which was purified by FC.
4-[(2-ethylbutyl)amino]-2-methyl-6-(pyridin-3-yl)quinoline-3-carbonitrile
as an off white solid (75 mg, 52%). m/z 345 (M+H)+.
