$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure Q: Methyl
1-(3-amino-6-(thiophen-2-yl)pyrazin-2-yl)piperidine-4-carboxylate (40h)
To a microwave vial was added aminobromopyrazine 39 (40 mg, 0.13 mmol),
thiophen-2-ylboronic acid (24 mg, 0.19 mmol), Pd(dppf)Cl2·CH2Cl2 (11 mg,
0.013 mmol), aqueous Na2CO3 solution (2M, 0.13 mL, 0.25 mmol) and DME
(0.5 mL). The reaction mixture was heated in a microwave for 1 h at 105
ºC. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo directly onto silica
gel. The residue was purified by flash column chromatography (12-50%
EtOAc in hexane) aminopyrazine 40h (20 mg, 50%) as a yellow residue: 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.07 (s, 1H), 7.43 (dd, J = 3.6, 1.1 Hz, 1H),
7.30-7.25 (m, 1H), 7.07 (dd, J = 5.0, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 4.65 (s (br), 2H),
3.73 (s, 3H), 3.64 (dt, J = 12.9, 3.0 Hz, 2H), 2.90 (dt, J = 12.9, 2.5
Hz, 2H), 2.08 (dd, J = 13.2, 3.6 Hz, 3H), 1.97-1.83 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (126
MHz, CDCl3) δ 175.3, 146.9, 146.0, 142.9, 136.9, 130.9, 127.8, 125.3,
