$DATUM 7-(3,4-Dihydro-2H-benzo[1,4]oxazin-7-yl)-3-(2,2,2-trifluoroethyl)imidazo[1,2-a]pyridine-8-carbonitrile
(27d). To a stirred suspension of 13e (0.18 g, 0.69 mmol) and 6a (0.16 g,
0.62 mmol) in a saturated aqueous solution of NaHCO3 (2 mL) and
1,4-dioxane (4 mL) was added Pd(PPh3)4 (0.036 g, 0.031 mmol). The mixture
was heated at 150 °C for 10 min under microwave irradiation. The mixture
was cooled to room temperature and filtered through a Celite pad. The
filtrate was diluted with water (20 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (2 × 15
mL). The organic layer was washed with brine (15 mL), dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was
purified by flash column chromatography (silica gel, EtOAc in heptane,
0/100 to 20/80) to give the desired product 27d. Yellow solid, yield
(0.11 mg, 50%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 3.36-3.40 (m, 2H), 4.17
(broad t, J= 4.4 Hz, 2H), 4.28 (q, J= 10.9 Hz, 2H), 6.45-6.48 (m, 1H),
6.72 (d, J= 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.13 (d, J= 2.3 Hz, 1H), 7.16 (dd, J= 8.2, 2.2
Hz, 1H), 7.25 (d, J= 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.70 (s, 1H), 8.80 (d, J= 7.4 Hz, 1H).
LC-MS: m/z 359 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Imidazo[1,2-a]pyridines: Orally Active Positive Allosteric Modulators of
the Metabotropic Glutamate 2 Receptor
