$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure 2. Optimization reactions under microwave conditions: A
solution of the electrophile 3 (372 mg, 1.00 mmol),
4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-2-(5-(trimethylstannyl)thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(1) (448 mg, 1.2 mmol), [Pd(PPh3)4] (20 mg, 2 mol%) and the internal
standard 1,3,5-triisopropylbenzene (100 μL, 86 mg, 0.43 mmol) in DMF (4
mL) was heated to 100 °C in a microwave apparatus. After 10, 20 and 30
minutes, a sample (0.1 mL) was taken from the reaction vessel, filtered
through a short plug of silica (5 x 3 mm; eluent: ethyl acetate) using a
syringe filter and was then used for GC analysis.
4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-2-(5-(5-bromo-3-n-hexylthiophen)thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(5b) 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.43 (d, 1H, 3 J = 3.6 Hz, Tph-H-b/c),
7.08 (d, 1H, 3 J = 3.6 Hz, Tph-H-b/c), 6.84 (s, 1H, Tph-H-f), 2.48-2.43
(m, 2H, Tph-CH2), 1.55-1.49 (m, 2H, Tph-CH2 CH 2), 1.29-1.27 (m, 18H,
Tph- (CH2)2(CH 2)3CH3, pin-C(CH 3)4), 0.82 (t, 3H, 3 J = 6.4 Hz, alkyl-CH
3) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 143.4 (Tph-C-e/h), 143.0
(Tph-C-e/h), 137.9 (Tph-CH-b/c), 136.6 (Tph-C-d), 132.3 (Tph-C-g), 125.1
(Tph-C-f), 124.8 (Tph-C-b/c), 108.4 (Tph-C-a), 84.2 (pin-C(CH3)4), 31.6,
29.6, 29.5, 28.8, 22.6 (Tph-(CH2)5CH3), 24.8 (pin-C(CH3)4), 14.1
(Tph-(CH2)5 CH3) ppm. 11B NMR (160 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 28.8 ppm. IR (ATR): ν
= 2926 (m), 2855 (w), 1523 (m), 1470 (s), 1425 (m), 1346 (s), 1286 (s),
1140 (s), 1065 (s), 1016 (m), 956 (w), 852 (s), 805 (m), 658 (w), 663 (s)
cm-1. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 456/454 (82)/(74) [M]+, 305 (100)
[M-Br-C5H11]+. MS (CI, isobutane): m/z (%) = 457/455 (65)/(76) [M + H]+,
456/454 (100)/(81) [M - H + H]+. HRMS (ESI): m/z found 455.0878; calcd.
for C20H29BBrO2S2 455.0879.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, Stille coupling, 1mol% of catalyst
used, similar result obtained with 2 mol% catalyst loading and 20min
reaction time, optimization study (based on catalyst loading, time and
temperature)
